# TCR05 : OCTO1170 : Test a CancelRequest that arrives before the M code of a query runs cancels the query
# A CancelRequest makes the rocto server send itself a signal, which YottaDB records as a pending job interrupt.
# The SimpleAPI calls made while a query is parsed and its plan generated discard a pending job interrupt. So a
# CancelRequest that arrived then used to be lost, and the query ran to completion. The signal handler of the rocto
# server now also sets ctrlc_pressed, which run_query() and handle_execute() check right before they run the M code
# of the query. The rocto server below sends itself the CancelRequest signal before it parses each query.
# Run a SELECT and an UPDATE through psql (simple query protocol). Expect both to be canceled.
ERROR:  canceling statement due to user request
ERROR:  canceling statement due to user request
# Run the same SELECT and UPDATE through JDBC (extended query protocol). Expect both to be canceled.
SQL State: 57014
ERROR: canceling statement due to user request
SQL State: 57014
ERROR: canceling statement due to user request
# Verify through octo that neither UPDATE changed the row
id|firstname|lastname
0|Zero|Cool
(1 row)
